IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `bsma-types`

-- Building (Strata Management) Act 2004 — GOAL 4: THE COUNCIL.
--
--   "May this person stand for the council or this office; has the member's
--    office been vacated or may the member be removed; is the council's
--    meeting quorate and its decision effective; and who answers for the
--    corporation's debts when it has no officers?"
--
-- Source: ../source/BSMA2004.txt — Part 5, Division 3 (ss 53-61), s 80, the
-- Second Schedule.

§ `Goal 4 — the council`

§§ `Size and eligibility (s 53)`

-- s 53(1): "in no case exceeding a total of 14 natural persons". (2): where
-- there are "not more than 3 subsidiary proprietors", the council is each
-- natural-person proprietor (or nominee) and each company's nominee.
-- s 26(3)(a): a council is elected "where there are more than 3".
@ref s 53(1)-(2)
GIVEN proprietors IS A NUMBER, `seats decided` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the council's size, proprietors` proprietors `, seats decided` `seats decided` MEANS
    BRANCH IF proprietors AT MOST 3       THEN proprietors
           IF `seats decided` GREATER THAN 14 THEN 14
           OTHERWISE                           `seats decided`

-- s 53(12): a multi-lot proprietor's "threshold number" is "(a) the number of
-- council members that is proportional to the subsidiary proprietor's share
-- value, ignoring any fraction; or (b) 49% of the number of council members
-- ..., ignoring any fraction, whichever number is lower".
@ref s 53(12)
GIVEN `share value` IS A NUMBER, aggregate IS A NUMBER, seats IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the threshold number, share value` `share value` `of` aggregate `, seats` seats MEANS
    IF `proportional` AT MOST `49 per cent` THEN `proportional` ELSE `49 per cent`
    WHERE
        `proportional` MEANS FLOOR (seats TIMES `share value` DIVIDED BY aggregate)
        `49 per cent`  MEANS FLOOR (seats TIMES 49 DIVIDED BY 100)

-- s 53(6): eligible only if "an individual of at least 21 years of age" and a
-- proprietor, a company proprietor's nominee, or an immediate family member
-- nominated by a proprietor. (7): not if the lot is in arrears "on the 3rd day
-- before the date of election". (8)(a): not a joint proprietor whose
-- co-proprietor also stands or nominates; (8)(b): not a nominee beyond the
-- threshold number. (9): an undischarged bankrupt only if the status "is
-- declared in writing ... at the time of his or her nomination". (9A): not to
-- one of chairperson, treasurer, secretary if already elected to another.
-- (9B): not as treasurer if that "would result in the person holding office
-- as a treasurer for 3 consecutive terms".
@ref s 53(6)-(9B), (12)
GIVEN c IS A Candidate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `eligible for election to the council` c IF
        c's `age` AT LEAST 21
    AND (NOT c's `capacity` EQUALS `none of these`)
    AND (NOT c's `arrears on the lot 3 days before the election`)
    AND (NOT c's `a joint proprietor whose co-proprietor also stands or nominates`)
    AND (NOT c's `the nominator's nominees exceed its threshold number`)
    AND ((NOT c's `an undischarged bankrupt`) OR c's `bankruptcy declared in writing at nomination`)
    AND `free of the office limits`
    WHERE
        `free of the office limits` MEANS
            CONSIDER c's `standing for`
            WHEN `an ordinary member` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `treasurer` THEN
                    (NOT c's `already elected to another of chairperson, secretary, treasurer`)
                AND c's `consecutive terms already served as treasurer` LESS THAN 2
            OTHERWISE NOT c's `already elected to another of chairperson, secretary, treasurer`

-- s 53A(3): a reserved council office for a class of use is open only to a
-- proprietor of a lot authorised for that use, or that proprietor's nominee.
-- (4)-(6): one eligible nominee is elected unopposed; none, and the office
-- ceases to be reserved; more, and a vote.
@ref s 53A(1), (3)
GIVEN proprietors IS A NUMBER, `classes of use` IS A NUMBER, `a proprietor or nominee of a lot of that class` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may stand for a reserved council office, proprietors` proprietors `, classes of use` `classes of use` `, of that class:` `a proprietor or nominee of a lot of that class` IF
    proprietors GREATER THAN 3 AND `classes of use` AT LEAST 2 AND `a proprietor or nominee of a lot of that class`

§§ `Vacation and removal (ss 54-55)`

-- s 54(1)(a)-(j): the member "must vacate" office — among others, on failing
-- "to attend 3 consecutive meetings of the council without having first
-- obtained ... permission" ((c)), or on a conviction for fraud or dishonesty
-- "on or after 1 April 2005" ((j)).
@ref s 54(1)
GIVEN e IS A `Vacating event`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the council member's office is vacated by` e IF
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `(c) missed council meetings without permission` n THEN n AT LEAST 3
    WHEN `(j) convicted of fraud or dishonesty` since2005 THEN since2005
    WHEN `none` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 54(2): removal "(a) without a general meeting" where the member's (or the
-- nominating proprietor's) contributions "are in arrears for more than
-- 3 months"; "(b) by ordinary resolution at a general meeting in any other
-- case".
@ref s 54(2)
GIVEN `months in arrears` IS A NUMBER, `an ordinary resolution at a general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the corporation may remove the council member, months in arrears` `months in arrears` `, ordinary resolution:` `an ordinary resolution at a general meeting` IF
    `months in arrears` GREATER THAN 3 OR `an ordinary resolution at a general meeting`

-- s 55(5): an officer "must not resign ... until ... a meeting of the council
-- is first convened for the purpose of appointing another person ... or ... a
-- general meeting is first convened for the purpose of electing another
-- person"; a resignation in breach "is deemed to be invalid".
@ref s 55(5)
GIVEN `a meeting to fill the office convened` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an officer's resignation is effective, meeting to replace convened:` `a meeting to fill the office convened` IF
    `a meeting to fill the office convened`

-- s 55(6): if the corporation "carries on business without any chairperson,
-- secretary and treasurer for more than 6 months", every proprietor who knows
-- it is jointly and severally liable for debts contracted after the 6 months.
@ref s 55(6)
GIVEN `months without officers` IS A NUMBER, `the proprietor knows` IS A BOOLEAN, `debt contracted after the 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proprietor is personally liable for the debt, months without officers` `months without officers` `, knows:` `the proprietor knows` `, debt after 6 months:` `debt contracted after the 6 months` IF
    `months without officers` GREATER THAN 6 AND `the proprietor knows` AND `debt contracted after the 6 months`

§§ `Council decisions (ss 58-60; Second Schedule)`

-- Second Schedule para 2(1): a quorum is "(a) where there is only one member
-- ... that member; or (b) where there are 2 or more members ... the majority
-- of the members". para 2(2): a member who cannot vote under s 60 is counted.
@ref Second Schedule para 2(1)-(2A)
GIVEN members IS A NUMBER, present IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the council meeting is quorate, members` members `, present` present IF
    IF members EQUALS 1 THEN present AT LEAST 1 ELSE (present TIMES 2) GREATER THAN members

-- s 58(1): a council decision is the corporation's decision, except on a
-- "restricted matter" (4): one needing a unanimous, special, 90%,
-- comprehensive or consensus resolution or a general meeting, or reserved
-- under s 59. (3): no effect if, before it is made, proprietors owning "not
-- less than one-third of the lots" gave written notice of opposition.
@ref s 58(1), (3)-(4)
GIVEN `a restricted matter` IS A BOOLEAN, `lots opposing in writing` IS A NUMBER, lots IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the council's decision binds the corporation, restricted matter:` `a restricted matter` `, lots opposing` `lots opposing in writing` `of` lots IF
    (NOT `a restricted matter`) AND (`lots opposing in writing` TIMES 3) LESS THAN lots

-- Second Schedule para 4(1): notice of a council meeting "at least 3 days
-- before the time fixed"; para 3(2): minutes displayed "not later than the
-- 14th day after the meeting" (council) or "45th day after the general
-- meeting", kept up "not less than 14 days" (3).
@ref Second Schedule para 3(2)
GIVEN `a general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN, meeting IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`minutes must be displayed by, general meeting:` `a general meeting` `, meeting` meeting MEANS
    IF `a general meeting` THEN meeting PLUS 45 ELSE meeting PLUS 14

-- Second Schedule para 7: a resolution in writing is valid if notice of the
-- intended meeting was given, the motion served on each member, "approved in
-- writing by a majority of members", and the matter is not one reserved to a
-- council meeting under s 59.
@ref Second Schedule para 7
GIVEN `notice given` IS A BOOLEAN, `motion served on each member` IS A BOOLEAN, approving IS A NUMBER, members IS A NUMBER, `reserved to a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the written council resolution is valid, notice:` `notice given` `, served:` `motion served on each member` `, approving` approving `of` members `, reserved:` `reserved to a meeting` IF
    `notice given` AND `motion served on each member` AND (approving TIMES 2) GREATER THAN members AND (NOT `reserved to a meeting`)

-- s 60(1): a member with a pecuniary interest must declare it, not take part or
-- vote, and withdraw if directed; (2) not where it is only membership of or
-- credit to a company and "not ... a material interest"; (8) an immediate
-- family member's interest is the member's.
@ref s 60(1)-(2), (8)
GIVEN `the member or family has a pecuniary interest` IS A BOOLEAN, `only a non-material company interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member must declare and abstain, interest:` `the member or family has a pecuniary interest` `, only non-material company interest:` `only a non-material company interest` IF
    `the member or family has a pecuniary interest` AND (NOT `only a non-material company interest`)

§§ `Provisions carried as text`

@ref ss 53(3)-(5), (10)-(11), 53A(2), (4)-(8), 54(3)-(4), 55(1)-(4), (7), 56, 57, 59, 60(3)-(9), 61, 80, Second Schedule paras 1, 1A, 3-6, 8
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`council provisions carried as text` MEANS
    LIST "s 53(3)-(5), (10)-(11): a sole proprietor decides as the council; the council is elected at each AGM and retires at the next; administration where there is no council"
         "s 53A(2), (4)-(8): reserved offices for mixed-use developments; filling the rest by votes; ties by lots"
         "ss 54(3)-(4), 55(1)-(4), (7): casual vacancies filled by the council with consent; officers' appointment and tenure"
         "ss 56, 57: the secretary's and treasurer's duties; who may handle money; delegation; joint performance orders"
         "s 60(3)-(9): general notices, conflicts from offices or property, minutes"
         "s 61: council members and officers must act honestly and diligently and not misuse position; liability and offence (Goal 6)"
         "s 80: subsidiary management corporations' meetings and executive committees"
         "Second Schedule: chairing, virtual meetings, records, notice boards, notice contents, adjournment, proprietors' attendance, validity despite vacancy, minutes"
